  mod_import_bare_err_ambiguous.pcpp - break step of mod_import_bare.pcpp:
  KShared named bare, while mod_import_bare_a and mod_import_bare_b both
  export it. No import order decides: write mod_import_bare_a.KShared or
  mod_import_bare_b.KShared (SM0020, a note at each unit's declaration).

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\mod_import_bare_err_ambiguous.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\mod_import_bare_err_ambiguous.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  The marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe mod_import_bare_err_ambiguous;
import mod_import_bare_a, mod_import_bare_b;

begin
  println("{}", KShared); // ERROR SM0020@17
end.
